{"collection":{"version":"1.1","href":"http://images-api.nasa.gov/search?q=Gemini+8+Agena+docking&media_type=image&year_start=1966&year_end=1966&page_size=25","items":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-25774/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-03-16T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-25774 (16 March 1966) --- The Agena Target Docking vehicle seen from the Gemini-8 spacecraft during rendezvous in space. The Agena is approximately 1,000 feet away from the nose of the spacecraft (lower left). Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["FLIGHT OPERATIONS","GEMINI 8 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","GEMINI SPACECRAFT","ONBOARD ACTIVITIES","PHOTOGRAPHY","SPACECRAFT DOCKING","TARGETS"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-25774","title":"Agena Target Docking vehicle seen from Gemini 8 spacecraft"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-25774/s66-25774~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":57000,"height":1242},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-25774/s66-25774~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":8500,"height":621},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-25774/s66-25774~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":8500,"height":621},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-25774/s66-25774~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":207000,"height":1864},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-25774/s66-25774~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-25778/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-03-16T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-25778 (16 March 1966) --? The Agena Target Docking Vehicle seen from the National Aeronautics and Space Administration?s Gemini-8 spacecraft during rendezvous in space. The Agena is approximately 260 feet away from the nose of the spacecraft (lower left). Crewmen for the Gemini-8 mission are astronauts Neil A. Armstrong, command pilot, and David R. Scott, pilot. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["FLIGHT OPERATIONS","GEMINI 8 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","GEMINI SPACECRAFT","ONBOARD ACTIVITIES","PHOTOGRAPHY","SPACECRAFT DOCKING","TARGETS"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-25778","title":"Agena Target Docking vehicle seen from Gemini 8 spacecraft"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-25778/s66-25778~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":42000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-25778/s66-25778~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":12000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-25778/s66-25778~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":12000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-25778/s66-25778~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":95000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-25778/s66-25778~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-25784/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-03-16T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-25784 (16 March 1966) --? The Agena Target Docking Vehicle seen from the National Aeronautics and Space Administration?s Gemini adapter of the Agena is approximately two feet from the nose of the spacecraft (lower left).  Crewmen for the Gemini-8 mission were astronauts Neil A. Armstrong, command pilot, and David R. Scott, pilot. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["FLIGHT OPERATIONS","GEMINI 8 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","GEMINI SPACECRAFT","ONBOARD ACTIVITIES","PHOTOGRAPHY","SPACECRAFT DOCKING","TARGETS"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-25784","title":"Agena Target Docking vehicle seen from Gemini 8 spacecraft"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-25784/s66-25784~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":100000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-25784/s66-25784~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":27000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-25784/s66-25784~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":27000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-25784/s66-25784~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":239000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-25784/s66-25784~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-24482/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-03-16T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-24482 (16 March 1966) --- An Agena Target Docking Vehicle atop an Atlas rocket lifts off from Launch Complex 14 at Cape Kennedy at 10 a.m., March 16, 1966 just prior to the Gemini-8 liftoff at nearby Launch Complex 19. The Agena served as a rendezvous and docking vehicle for the Gemini-8 spacecraft. A chase plane leaves a contrail in the background. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S66-24482","title":"LIFTOFF - GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-8 - ATLAS/AGENA - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-24482/S66-24482~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":173000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-24482/S66-24482~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":47000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-24482/S66-24482~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":47000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-24482/S66-24482~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":387000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-24482/S66-24482~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/9141928/collection.json","data":[{"center":"MSFC","date_created":"1966-03-16T00:00:00Z","description":"On March 16, 1966, an Atlas booster launched an Agena Target Vehicle for the Gemini 8 mission. The flight crew for the 3 day mission, astronauts Neil A. Armstrong and David R. Scott, achieved the first rendezvous and docking to Atlas/Agena in Earth orbit.","keywords":["Atlas-Agena","Launch"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"9141928","title":"Early Rockets"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/9141928/9141928~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":969,"size":124000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/9141928/9141928~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":484,"size":33000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/9141928/9141928~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":484,"size":33000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/9141928/9141928~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1454,"size":274000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/9141928/9141928~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-25779/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-03-16T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-25779 (16 March 1966) --? The Agena Target Docking Vehicle seen from the National Aeronautics and Space Administration?s Gemini-8 spacecraft during rendezvous in space. The Agena is approximately 210 feet away from the nose of the spacecraft (lower left). Crewmen for the Gemini-8 mission were astronauts Neil A. Armstrong, command pilot, and David R. Scott, pilot. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["GEMINI 8 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","AGENA ROCKET VEHICLES"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-25779","title":"Gemini VIII Mission Image - Agena"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-25779/s66-25779~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","