66) --- Closer view of the Agena Target Docking vehicle seen from the Gemini-8 spacecraft during rendezvous in space. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["GEMINI 8 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","AGENA ROCKET VEHICLES"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S66-25782","title":"Gemini VIII Mission Image - Agena"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-25782/S66-25782~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":84000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-25782/S66-25782~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":26000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-25782/S66-25782~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":26000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-25782/S66-25782~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":168000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-25782/S66-25782~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-24465/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-03-16T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-24465 (16 March 1966) --- The Gemini-Titan 8 (GT-8), carrying astronauts Neil A. Armstrong, command pilot, and David R. Scott, pilot, was successfully launched by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration's (NASA) John F. Kennedy Space Center (KSC) at 11:41 a.m. (EST), March 16, 1966. An attempt will be made to rendezvous and dock the Gemini-8 spacecraft with Agena Docking Target Vehicle. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S66-24465","title":"LIFTOFF - GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-8 - ATLAS/AGENA - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-24465/S66-24465~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":581,"size":59000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-24465/S66-24465~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":290,"size":16000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-24465/S66-24465~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":290,"size":16000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-24465/S66-24465~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/9141927/collection.json","data":[{"center":"MSFC","date_created":"1966-03-16T00:00:00Z","description":"A Titan booster launched the Gemini 8 spacecraft on March 16, 1966 from launch complex 19 Cape Kennedy, Florida. The flight crew for the 3 day mission, astronauts Neil A. Armstrong and David R. Scott, achieved the first rendezvous and docking to Atlas/Agena in Earth orbit.","keywords":["Gemini 8","Titan","Atlas/Agena"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"9141927","title":"Early Rockets"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/9141927/9141927~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1005,"size":84000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/9141927/9141927~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":502,"size":18000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/9141927/9141927~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":502,"size":18000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/9141927/9141927~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1507,"size":231000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/9141927/9141927~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/KSC-66PC-0038/collection.json","data":[{"center":"KSC","date_created":"1966-03-16T00:00:00Z","description":"CAPE KENNEDY, Fla. -- At Cape Kennedy Air Force Station in Florida, Gemini 8 lifts off atop a Titan II rocket with command pilot Neil A. Armstrong and pilot David R. Scott aboard. They plan to rendezvous and dock with an Agena target satellite and Scott will perform a spacewalk. Photo Credit: NASA","keywords":["Kennedy History"],"location":"Kennedy Space Center, FL","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"KSC-66PC-0038","title":"KSC-66PC-0038"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/KSC-66PC-0038/KSC-66PC-0038~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":167000,"height":1024},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/KSC-66PC-0038/KSC-66PC-0038~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":43000,"height":512},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/KSC-66PC-0038/KSC-66PC-0038~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":43000,"height":512},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/KSC-66PC-0038/KSC-66PC-0038~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":431000,"height":1536},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/KSC-66PC-0038/KSC-66PC-0038~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image","height":2400,"width":3000,"size":2200000}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-18616/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-03-16T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-18616 (16 March 1966) --- Gemini-Titan 8 (GT-8) spacecraft, carrying astronauts Neil A. Armstrong, command pilot, and David R. Scott, pilot, was successfully launched by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration's (NASA) John F. Kennedy Space Center (KSC) at 11:41 a.m. (EST), March 16, 1966. An attempt will be made to rendezvous and dock the GT-8 spacecraft with Agena Docking Target Vehicle. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S66-18616","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-8 - ATLAS/AGENA - LIFTOFF - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-18616/S66-18616~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":588,"size":64000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-18616/S66-18616~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":294,"size":20000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-18616/S66-18616~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":294,"size":20000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-18616/S66-18616~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-46025/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-07-18T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-46025 (18 July 1966) --- Astronaut Michael Collins, Gemini-10 pilot, photographed this MSC-8 color patch outside the spacecraft during the Gemini-10/Agena docking mission. The experiment was for the purpose of showing what effect the environment of space will have upon the color photography taken in cislunar space and on the lunar surface during an Apollo mission. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["GEMINI 10 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","LOGO","ONBOARD ACTIVITIES","PHOTOGRAPHY","SPACECRAFT DOCKING","TESTS"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-46025","title":"Photograph of MSC-8 color patch outside spacecraft during docking"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-46025/s66-46025~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":48000,"height":1261},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-46025/s66-46025~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":13000,"height":630},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-46025/s66-46025~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":13000,"height":630},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-46025/s66-46025~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":144000,"height":1891},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-46025/s66-46025~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]}],"metadata":{"total_hits":13}}}